  "steps": [
    "<strong>Curry:</strong> Heat butter and oil in a wide pan over medium heat. Add onion and cook 10 minutes until very soft and lightly golden.",
    "Add garlic and ginger; cook 1 minute until fragrant.",
    "Stir in garam masala, cumin, and paprika. Toast briefly.",
    "Add tomato purée, then chopped tomatoes. Simmer 10 minutes until thickened.",
    "Stir in chickpeas and cream or coconut milk. Simmer 10–15 minutes until rich and cohesive.",
    "Season with salt, a small pinch of sugar, and lemon juice to balance.",
    "<strong>Paneer / Seitan:</strong> Cut into bite-size pieces.",
    "Heat oil in a pan and fry until deeply golden on all sides. Season lightly with salt and paprika.",
    "Reheat curry gently and stir paneer or seitan in just before serving to preserve texture."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Adding the paneer at the end keeps it crisp and prevents it from going rubbery.",
    "This curry tastes even better the next day as the flavours deepen.",
    "Serve with basmati rice, naan, or roti."
  ]
